menu "ThorVG"

    config RIVE_THORVG_THREADS
        bool "Enable ThorVG task scheduler threads"
        default n
        help
            Builds ThorVG with its std::thread based task scheduler. Not
            used by this project: both cores are already used by rendering
            the frame in two lanes (Rive player -> Render on both CPU cores),
            and the player starts ThorVG without worker threads. Leave off.

    config RIVE_THORVG_FAST_GRADIENT
        bool "Faster linear-gradient spans"
        default y
        help
            Replaces ThorVG's per-pixel blend-operator call and spread-mode
            switch in linear-gradient spans with loops specialised per
            operator (components/thorvg/fast). Pixel-identical output.
            Turn off to compare against stock ThorVG.

    config RIVE_THORVG_SKIP_PARTIAL_CLEAR
        bool "Skip the dirty-region clear under an opaque background"
        default y
        help
            With partial redraw, ThorVG clears each changed region before
            redrawing it. The Rive player always draws an opaque full-frame
            background first, so that clear is redundant memory traffic.
            Pixel-identical output. Only applies while the clear colour is
            opaque.

    config RIVE_THORVG_RLE_CELL_PERCENT
        int "Scanline cell buffer size (% of ThorVG's default)"
        range 75 800
        default 200
        help
            ThorVG converts each shape outline to coverage spans in
            horizontal bands sized to fit a cell buffer of max(w, h) * 0.75
            cells. A band that needs more cells is discarded, halved and
            redone. 200 (twice the default size) avoids almost all of those
            restarts at 720x720 (about 20% less span-generation work), for
            about 29 KB per render lane (in PSRAM). Output is identical.
            75 = stock ThorVG.

    config RIVE_THORVG_HOT_IRAM
        bool "Experiment: run hot raster code from internal RAM"
        default n
        help
            Places ThorVG's hottest raster functions (the outline
            rasteriser and the gradient / solid span loops, about 17 KB) in
            IRAM instead of executing them from PSRAM through the caches
            (components/thorvg/linker.lf). Costs that much internal RAM,
            which is scarce once an animation is loaded. Measured on the
            car at 720 (2026-11-02): 14.4-14.5 fps off, 14.6 on, shape RLE
            and fill within 1-2% (the hot loops already stay in the
            instruction cache), so it's off by default.

endmenu
